{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>My myrrh</b> [etc. — the phrase is not fully cited; the lemma refers to the cluster of henna in the verse]: A cluster of henna. In the language of Kedar: כאפור, and in the language [of another locale]: כאנפורא, and it is like clusters. And some say it is a species of clove, and the first [opinion] is closer." "In the vineyards of Ein Gedi. A place name [in the land of Israel, where the cluster of henna would be found]."], :book :song-of-songs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {0 "The lemma head reads 'הפעם הא׳' (the fifth time), apparently a cross-reference to a word discussed for the fifth time rather than a quotation of the verse; the body discusses אשכל הכופר from Song 1:14."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra's commentary on the Canticles" "http://beta.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH002030344/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:43:53.375208418Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}